## 189 - Rotate Array by K places

## Approach
1. First I find k % n because if k is greater than the array length,
   we only need the remaining rotations.
2. I reverse the complete array.
3. Then I reverse the first k elements to put the last k elements
   in their correct order.
4. Finally, I reverse the remaining elements to put them in their
   correct order.

Example:
[1,2,3,4,5,6,7], k = 3

Reverse whole array:
[7,6,5,4,3,2,1]

Reverse first k elements:
[5,6,7,4,3,2,1]

Reverse remaining elements:
[5,6,7,1,2,3,4]

So the array is rotated to the right by k positions.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public void rotate(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;
        k = k % n;
        arrayRotate(nums, 0, n - 1);
        arrayRotate(nums, 0, k - 1);
        arrayRotate(nums, k, n - 1);
    }

    public void arrayRotate(int[] arr, int start, int end) {
        while (start < end) {
            int temp = arr[start];
            arr[start] = arr[end];
            arr[end] = temp;
            start++;
            end--;
        }
    }

}
